# gh CLI's vendored golang.org/x/mod/sumdb (Go module checksum-db
# verification); upstream has not yet released a build with the fix.
# Confirmed no usage of golang.org/x/mod in cli/cli's own source (GitHub
# code search) — only reachable via `gh extension` Go-module tooling,
# which djimitflo's GithubPrReviewService never invokes (only pr view/
# diff/comment and api). Revisit when cli/cli ships a release past
# v2.100.0 with the dependency bumped.
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

# gh CLI (/usr/bin/gh) is built with Go stdlib 1.26.8 (v2.100.0) / 1.27.1 (latest v2.102.0); both CVEs are fixed only in
# 1.26.9 / 1.27.2 and no gh release ships those yet. Both are denial-of-service bugs in SERVER code paths:
# CVE-2026-78667 net/http Range-header handling when serving content, CVE-2026-97031 crypto/tls ECH outer-extension
# processing of a ClientHello. djimitflo runs gh only as an HTTPS client (pr view / pr diff / comment / api in
# GithubPrReviewService, github-cocreate); it never serves HTTP or terminates TLS with gh. Revisit when cli/cli ships a
# release built with Go >= 1.27.2 (then bump GH_CLI_VERSION in the Dockerfile and drop these lines).
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031

# gh CLI (/usr/bin/gh): golang.org/x/net v0.58.0 + Go stdlib 1.26.8 carry CVE-2026-78669 (HTTP/2 denial of service via
# excessive SETTINGS frames), fixed in x/net 0.60.0 / Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2; no gh release ships them yet (latest v2.102.0 is
# built with Go 1.27.1). djimitflo runs gh only as a short-lived HTTPS client against api.github.com (GithubPrReviewService,
# github-cocreate); it never serves HTTP/2, and the only peer that could send SETTINGS frames is GitHub itself. Revisit with
# the two entries above when cli/cli ships a release with the fixes (bump GH_CLI_VERSION, drop these lines).
CVE-2026-78669
